CAT = "fladjLiability"; SEG = "LIA"
Q = [
("CGL Coverage A excludes bodily injury to the insured's own employees in the course of their work because that exposure belongs under:",
 "Workers' comp and employers liability", ["Coverage C medical payments to others", "A commercial umbrella only", "Professional liability"],
 "The CGL's employer's liability exclusion sends work injuries to employees to the workers compensation and employers liability policy."),
("Under CGL Coverage C, medical expenses must be incurred and reported within how long after the accident?",
 "One year", ["Three years", "90 days", "Two years"],
 "The commercial general liability form pays Coverage C expenses incurred and reported within one year of the accident date."),
("Which offense is covered under CGL Coverage B, personal and advertising injury?",
 "Malicious prosecution", ["A customer slip and fall", "Damage to a rented car", "Injury from a defective toy"],
 "Coverage B covers listed offenses such as false arrest, malicious prosecution, wrongful eviction, libel, slander and copyright infringement in an advertisement. Slip and fall and product injuries are Coverage A bodily injury."),
("A claims-made CGL policy covers a claim only if it is:",
 "First made during the policy period", ["Caused during any earlier policy year", "Reported within ten years", "Settled before expiration"],
 "A claims-made form is triggered by a claim first made during the policy period (or an extended reporting period) for injury after any retroactive date."),
("Under the CGL, the cost to withdraw defective products from the market is excluded by the:",
 "Product recall exclusion", ["Your work exclusion", "Pollution exclusion", "Contractual exclusion"],
 "The recall of products, work or impaired property exclusion bars the cost of withdrawing, inspecting or replacing products; recall coverage is sold separately."),
("On the CGL, the products-completed operations aggregate limit is:",
 "Separate from the general aggregate", ["Included within the occurrence limit", "Used only for premises claims", "Used for employee injuries"],
 "The CGL has a general aggregate for most claims and a separate products-completed operations aggregate, so a product loss does not erode the premises limit."),
("The CGL 'damage to premises rented to you' limit mainly covers:",
 "Fire damage to rented premises", ["The landlord's lost rent", "The tenant's own contents", "Injury to the landlord on a visit"],
 "The exception to the property damage exclusions pays for damage by fire to premises rented to the insured, and other damage to premises rented for 7 days or less, up to this limit."),
("The standard CGL pollution exclusion generally does not apply to bodily injury caused by:",
 "Smoke from a hostile fire", ["Fumes from a waste dump", "Chemicals spilled at a job", "A leaking fuel tank"],
 "The pollution exclusion has an exception for bodily injury or property damage from heat, smoke or fumes from a hostile fire, one that becomes uncontrollable or breaks out from where it was meant to be."),
("Employment practices liability insurance covers claims of:",
 "Wrongful termination", ["Workplace back injuries", "Unpaid overtime wages", "Employee theft of cash"],
 "EPL covers claims such as discrimination, harassment and wrongful termination. Work injuries are workers' compensation, overtime claims are usually excluded, and theft is crime coverage."),
("Professional liability (errors and omissions) insurance responds to claims of:",
 "Negligent professional services", ["Bodily injury on the business premises", "Accidents in company cars", "Theft by an employee"],
 "E&O covers financial harm from negligent acts, errors or omissions in rendering professional services, usually on a claims-made basis."),
("Homeowners Coverage F, medical payments to others, does not pay for injury to:",
 "A regular resident of the household", ["A guest who trips on the front stairs", "A neighbor bitten by the dog", "A child hurt in the yard"],
 "Coverage F pays others hurt on the insured location or by an insured's activities, but not the named insured or regular residents of the household other than residence employees."),
("Homeowners Section II liability excludes injury arising from an insured's:",
 "Business activities", ["Dog on a walk", "Golf swing at a club", "Bicycle ride in town"],
 "The homeowners policy excludes liability arising out of business and professional services; personal activities anywhere in the world are covered."),
("Equipment breakdown coverage pays for an accident, meaning a:",
 "Sudden breakdown of covered equipment", ["Gradual wear of a machine over many years", "Fire spreading from a neighbor", "Theft of a part from a machine"],
 "Equipment breakdown (formerly boiler and machinery) covers sudden and accidental breakdown of covered equipment that causes physical damage needing repair. Wear and tear is excluded and fire and theft belong to property coverage."),
("A service included with equipment breakdown insurance that most property policies do not provide is:",
 "Required boiler inspections", ["Flood cover for machinery", "Business auto liability", "Ocean cargo protection"],
 "Equipment breakdown insurers perform the jurisdictional inspections of boilers and pressure vessels that state law requires, and loss control inspections."),
("Commercial crime money orders and counterfeit money coverage pays when the insured:",
 "Accepts fake currency in good faith", ["Loses cash to a robber", "Has a check signature forged by a thief", "Wires funds to a fraudster"],
 "This insuring agreement covers money orders that are not paid and counterfeit currency the insured accepted in good faith in exchange for goods or services. Robbery, forgery and wire fraud have their own agreements."),
("A payment bond on a construction project guarantees that:",
 "Subcontractors and suppliers get paid", ["The project is finished on time", "The low bidder will sign the contract", "The owner pays the contractor"],
 "A payment bond protects those who supply labor and materials if the contractor fails to pay them; a performance bond guarantees completion and a bid bond that the bidder signs the contract."),
]
